# Settings for tools/check.sh in this project. This file is yours, and a
# sync never touches it. Write one KEY=VALUE per line. A # starts a comment.
# check.sh takes each value as written, with no $ expansion. A variable
# already set when check.sh starts (like one a CI workflow passes) wins over
# the line here.

# check.sh fails the boot when the game uses this much memory or more, in
# KB. The default is 400000 (about 390 MB). Raise it as the game grows.
# CHECK_RSS_BUDGET_KB=400000
